{"files":[{"content":"#include <cassert>\n#include <climits>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#include <omp.h>\n#endif\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const std::size_t row_width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(row_width * row_width);\n    for (int r = 0; r < n; ++r) {\n        int* row = matrix.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * row_width;\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n            if (std::scanf(\"%d\", &row[c]) != 1) return 0;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long max_sum = LLONG_MIN;\n\n    if (s == 1) {\n        const int element_count = n * n;\n        #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:max_sum) schedule(static) if(n >= 512)\n        for (int index = 0; index < element_count; ++index) {\n            const long long value = matrix[static_cast<std::size_t>(index)];\n            if (value > max_sum) max_sum = value;\n        }\n    } else {\n        const int window_count = n - s + 1;\n\n        #pragma omp parallel reduction(max:max_sum)\n        {\n            int team_size = 1;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n            team_size = omp_get_num_threads();\n#endif\n\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static, 1)\n            for (int block = 0; block < team_size; ++block) {\n                const int first = static_cast<int>(\n                    static_cast<long long>(window_count) * block / team_size);\n                const int last = static_cast<int>(\n                    static_cast<long long>(window_count) * (block + 1) / team_size);\n\n                if (first < last) {\n                    std::vector<long long> vertical(row_width, 0);\n\n                    for (int r = first; r < first + s; ++r) {\n                        const int* row = matrix.data() +\n                                         static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * row_width;\n                        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                            vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)] += row[c];\n                        }\n                    }\n\n                    for (int top = first; top < last; ++top) {\n                        if (top > first) {\n                            const int* leaving = matrix.data() +\n                                static_cast<std::size_t>(top - 1) * row_width;\n                            const int* entering = matrix.data() +\n                                static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s - 1) * row_width;\n                            for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                                vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)] +=\n                                    static_cast<long long>(entering[c]) - leaving[c];\n                            }\n                        }\n\n                        long long sum = 0;\n                        for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) {\n                            sum += vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(c)];\n                        }\n                        if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n\n                        for (int left = 1; left < window_count; ++left) {\n                            sum += vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(left + s - 1)] -\n                                   vertical[static_cast<std::size_t>(left - 1)];\n                            if (sum > max_sum) max_sum = sum;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", max_sum);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A dedicated parallel maximum scan for S=1 avoids the rolling-sum machinery when each window contains one value; for S>1, the measured top-row-block rolling-sum approach remains the general path. The controller should evaluate this integration end to end.","notes":"No commands or measurements were run; the controller should verify correctness and performance.","sources_kept":["3945be75cb784f83","3d696cf87ec64628"],"transformations":["Use contiguous row-major storage and scanf input; for S>1, partition top-row windows into balanced blocks with private rolling vertical sums, 64-bit accumulators, and an OpenMP max reduction.","For S=1, use a direct parallel maximum scan with 64-bit intermediates, enabling parallel execution for larger matrices."]}